            <ArticleTitle>MR imaging of exercise-induced lower leg pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>533-52, x</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>MR imaging of the lower leg is frequently performed to evaluate the active patient who presents with an exercise-induced injury. This article discusses both common and obscure osseous and soft tissue conditions that are seen in the athletic population with leg pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
